I walk away from the market and find a small, local museum.
I walk into the quiet building.
I walk over to the counter to buy an entrance ticket.
A young man is standing behind the register.
"Hi, one adult ticket, please," I say.
"That will be one hundred kroner," he says and prints it.
I pay and look at these colorful brochures on the counter.
They advertise a special exhibition about the history of the city.
"Does this ticket also give access to the exhibition upstairs?" I ask.
"Yes, this museum only has one combined ticket," he answers.
"The exhibition is upstairs on the first floor," he says.
"You can take your time up there."
"It has many old photographs of the city," he explains.
"Some of them are over a hundred years old."
"That sounds really exciting," I say.
"Thank you very much," I smile.
I take my ticket and walk calmly up the stairs.
